# {{.Name}}

Fiber v3 · templ · htmx{{if .Postgres}} · PostgreSQL (pgx){{end}}{{if .Redis}} · Redis{{end}}{{if .WebSocket}} · WebSocket{{end}}{{if .Tailwind}} · Tailwind CSS{{end}}{{if .Alpine}} · Alpine.js{{end}}{{if .Shadcn}} · shadcn/ui{{end}}{{if .React}} · React + Vite + TypeScript{{end}}

## Quick start

```bash
{{- if .Compose}}
make db-up      # start {{if and .Postgres .Redis}}Postgres and Redis{{else if .Postgres}}Postgres{{else}}Redis{{end}} in Docker
{{- end}}
make dev        # live reload: open http://localhost:5173
```

The app listens on `:3000`; `make dev` additionally starts the templ live-reload proxy on `:5173`.
If dependencies or tools are missing (for example you used `--skip-install`), run `make setup` once.

## Make targets

| Target | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `make setup` | install tools, front-end assets and dependencies, run `go mod tidy` |
| `make dev` | live development: templ watch{{if .Tailwind}} + Tailwind watch{{end}}{{if .Shadcn}} + shadcn bundle watch{{end}}{{if .React}} + Vite build watch{{end}} |
| `make build` | generate templ code{{if .Tailwind}}, build CSS{{end}}{{if .React}}, build React{{end}} and compile into `bin/server` |
| `make run` | build and run |
| `make htmx` | re-download htmx (it is committed in `static/js`) |
{{- if .Alpine}}
| `make alpine` | download Alpine.js into `static/js/alpine.min.js` |
{{- end}}
{{- if .Tailwind}}
| `make css` | build `static/css/app.css` from `web/input.css` |
{{- end}}
{{- if .Shadcn}}
| `make ui-add c="dialog tabs"` | add shadcn/ui components to `views/ui` |
| `make ui-bundle` | rebuild the JS bundle of the installed components |
{{- end}}
{{- if .React}}
| `make react-install` / `react-build` / `react-dev` | install, build or watch `frontend/` |
{{- end}}
{{- if .Compose}}
| `make db-up` / `db-down` / `db-logs` | manage the Docker services |
| `make db-reset` | recreate the services **and wipe their volumes** |
{{- end}}

## Project layout

```
cmd/main.go              entrypoint
internal/config          env config
internal/handlers        HTTP handlers and routes
{{- if .Postgres}}
internal/db              pgx pool
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}
internal/cache           redis client
{{- end}}
{{- if .WebSocket}}
internal/ws              broadcast hub for WebSocket clients
{{- end}}
views/                   ALL UI lives here (*_templ.go is generated)
  layouts/               page shells (<html>, <head>, scripts)
  pages/                 one templ per page
  components/            reusable pieces
{{- if .Shadcn}}
  ui/                    shadcn/ui components (generated by shadcn-templ)
  utils/                 helpers used by shadcn/ui components
{{- end}}
{{- if .Tailwind}}
web/input.css            Tailwind entry file
{{- end}}
{{- if .Shadcn}}
components.json         shadcn-templ configuration
{{- end}}
{{- if .React}}
frontend/                React + TypeScript + Vite (builds to static/react/app.js)
{{- end}}
static/                  served at /static
```

## Configuration (`.env`)

| Variable | Default |
| --- | --- |
| `PORT` | `3000` |
| `APP_ENV` | `development` (`production` enables static caching) |
{{- if .Postgres}}
| `DATABASE_URL` | `postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/{{.DBName}}?sslmode=disable` |
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}
| `REDIS_URL` | `redis://localhost:6379/0` |
{{- end}}
{{- if .WebSocket}}

## WebSocket

`GET /ws` upgrades to a WebSocket (`github.com/gofiber/contrib/v3/websocket`). Everything a client sends is broadcast to all connected clients by `internal/ws`. See `internal/handlers/ws.go` and the demo card on the home page.
{{- end}}
{{- if .React}}

## React

React lives in `frontend/` and is built by Vite into `static/react/app.js`. A templ component mounts it with a plain element:

```templ
<div data-react="Counter" data-props='{"title":"Hello"}'></div>
```

Register components in `frontend/src/main.tsx`. The demo calls the Go endpoint `GET /api/hello` (`internal/handlers/api.go`); the base URL is set in `frontend/src/api.ts` (`VITE_API_URL`, empty = same origin).
{{- end}}
{{- if .Shadcn}}

## shadcn/ui

Components come from [shadcn-templ](https://shadcn-templ.com) and are written into `views/ui` (see `components.json`). Use them in any templ file:

```templ
import "{{.Module}}/views/ui/button"

@button.Button(button.Props{Variant: button.VariantOutline}) { Click me }
```
{{- end}}
